What do you think?  How much do you think the overall quality of the
YANIs in these collections influences RGRN readers decisions to read
future collections at all?

[16]: Being swallowed should end your engraving. (unless you realy are
busily engraving in the belly of the beast). --assended

What if you continued your engraving on the inside of the monster?
"You are burning to a crisp!  Something is written here.  It says
'bereth'"

[17]: If you're sick when you get engulfed, you should be poisonous and
deal damage to the monster engulfing you. --azgor

:-D  I like this one.  Well, I always like my own ideas.  Too bad few
folks on RGRN share my opinions of them. :-(

